{"id": "EUVD-2026-69235", "enisaUuid": "597ec499-1bc2-3414-bce0-bae3a34ce22e", "description": "httpd function check_header/3 rejects duplicate Content-Length (per CVE-2026-23941) but never checks for the TE+CL co-presence that RFC 9112 \u00a76.3 identifies as a probable smuggling attempt. handle_body/3 frames by chunked and silently discards Content-Length. A CL-preferring front-end paired with chunked-preferring inets creates a classic CL.TE front-end/back-end desync.\n\nThis issue affects OTP from OTP\u00a017.0 before OTP\u00a027.3.4.17, from OTP\u00a028.0 before OTP\u00a028.5.0.6, and from OTP\u00a029.0 before OTP\u00a029.0.6, corresponding to inets from 5.10 before 9.3.2.7, from 9.4 before 9.6.2.3, and from 9.7 before 9.7.2. Whether OTP before OTP\u00a017.0, corresponding to inets before 5.10, is affected is unknown.", "datePublished": "2026-09-01T14:42:42", "dateUpdated": "2026-09-08T01:10:14", "baseScore": 8.3, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:P/PR:N/UI:N/VC:L/VI:H/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/erlang/otp/security/advisories/GHSA-7j6m-4ffg-hg46", "https://cna.erlef.org/cves/CVE-2026-73812.html", "https://osv.dev/vulnerability/EEF-CVE-2026-73812", "https://github.com/erlang/otp/commit/591dc00dc99dc2a426167a3b5257c0c94bd45e91"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-73812"], "assigner": "EEF", "epss": 0.52, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "2057d361-cecd-3c6a-9443-bfc4bab8924b", "product": {"name": "otp", "vendor": {"name": "erlang"}}, "product_version": "9.4 <9.6.2.3"}, {"id": "2c7e936f-c508-33e9-968c-3281e26dd351", "product": {"name": "otp", "vendor": {"name": "erlang"}}, "product_version": "29.0 <29.0.6"}, {"id": "4fe63911-da89-3601-917e-8afc0a7f0c59", "product": {"name": "otp", "vendor": {"name": "erlang"}}, "product_version": "84adefa331c4159d432d22840663c38f155cd4c1 <591dc00dc99dc2a426167a3b5257c0c94bd45e91"}, {"id": "561b3a8f-ed4e-3073-8559-faf91f535e26", "product": {"name": "otp", "vendor": {"name": "erlang"}}, "pr